-- title:
--   ℚ̄ is 𝒪 localised away from p
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a valuation subring of an algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $p$ be a natural number which is prime. Assume `O.LiesOverPrime p`, that is, the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ belongs to `O.nonunits`: $p$ lies in $O$ and is not a unit there, equivalently $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of the local ring $O$. The conclusion is `IsLocalization.Away` for the element $p$ of $O$ (the image of the natural number $p$ under the canonical map $\mathbb{N} \to O$) with value algebra $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: the inclusion $O \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ exhibits $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ as the localisation of $O$ at the multiplicative submonoid generated by $p$. Concretely this asserts three things: every power of $p$ becomes a unit in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; every $z \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ can be written as $a/p^{n}$ with $a \in O$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}$; and two elements of $O$ with the same image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ are annihilated by a common power of $p$. In short, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = O[1/p]$.
--
--   For a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $p$, the valuation ring becomes the whole field after inverting $p$; this is the arithmetic shape of the rank-one (archimedean value group) property of such valuations. It is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.isOpenImmersion_specMap_subtype_of_liesOverPrime`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.isOpenImmersion_specMap_subtype_of_liesOverPrime), where it identifies the generic fibre over such a valuation ring as an open subscheme.
